<p><a href="https://issuu.com/changingireland/docs/issue29"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Issue-29.png" alt="" width="568" height="802" srcset="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Issue-29.png 568w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Issue-29-212x300.png 212w" sizes="(max-width: 568px) 100vw, 568px" /></a></p>', 'Ireland has won a United Nations award for its response at community level to the Covid pandemic. The UN received over 350 entries from 58 countries for 10 awards – with Ireland winning one for its Social Inclusion and Community Activation Programme (SICAP).', 'https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Ireland-wins-UN-award-for-community-work.png', '', '[{"slug":"inclusion","title":"Inclusion"},{"slug":"programmes","title":"Programmes"}]', '[{"slug":"sicapstories","title":"#SicapStories"},{"slug":"sicap-social-inclusion-community-activation-programme","title":"SICAP"},{"slug":"united-nations","title":"United Nations"}]', '', 251990, 1, '2022-06-23T15:20:43Z', '2022-07-15T01:57:09Z', '2022-06-23T15:20:43Z')
